Eight commits from Mesa main for the NVK driver and the Vulkan runtime it is built with, in no Mesa release yet
(26.3.0 does not have them). Upstream text (MIT licence), unchanged, oldest first; the two lines commit c9ce420e removes
from CI fail lists (src/nouveau/ci, not part of the build) are left out:
  commit 0f737d4e nvk: fix color_write_enable
  commit fe4e33ab nvk: fix range calculation for map sync
  commit 617f463e nvk: only upload descriptor state if dirty
  commit 3e4d14a1 vulkan: Add vk_image_format_info_2_stencil_usage(..)
  commit 3ff6450e nvk: Include stencil usage in image format queries
  commit f924c7c9 nvk: limit push descriptor set upload to max_buffer_size
  commit db5503a2 vulkan: initialize swapchain private mutex properly
  commit c9ce420e vulkan: fix lookup of VkRenderingAttachmentLocationInfo
Why each one is here:
  color_write_enable: the MME macro added where it meant to mask, so SET_SINGLE_CT_WRITE_CONTROL was never turned on
  even when every render target had the same write mask; the output was right, the faster mode was never used.
  map sync range: the flush range of an indirect execution set update counted from slot 0 instead of the first slot
  written. No effect on the NVRM back end today (every NVRM memory is coherent), kept so the code matches upstream.
  push descriptor upload: the dirty mask of push descriptor sets was never cleared, so every draw or dispatch flush
  uploaded every push set again (upstream: 30 thousand fewer uploads a second in Deep Rock Galactic); and each upload
  copies the layout's size of the set, not the whole fixed-size array. Zink, DXVK and the DLSS passes use push sets.
  stencil usage: image format queries ignored VkImageStencilUsageCreateInfo and the usage2 structures in pNext;
  the helper it calls is the one commit 3e4d14a1 adds (an inline function in vk_physical_device.h, nothing else).
  swapchain private mutex: the mutex of vkGet/SetPrivateData on swapchains was initialised only on Android; on macOS
  a zeroed pthread mutex is not an initialised one, so that lock did not lock.
  rendering attachment locations: VkRenderingAttachmentLocationInfo of a secondary command buffer was looked for in
  the begin info instead of its inheritance info, so the remapping of attachments in it was lost.
Not taken: the NAK compiler changes on main (they change the code of shaders), f989f044 (vk_meta integer clamping:
only drivers that set sw_clamp_int_blits use it and NVK does not), 6712a065 (it changes a function that is only called
inside assert(), which a release build compiles out), afe1e0d5 (submit thread affinity: it needs the util helper of
commit 45abb7ce, which sets the affinity with pthread_setaffinity_np, and macOS has no such call).

